WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
London, 1802.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.400
Midday.

3
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.380
Brown haze, crowds, and
the rattle of cart wheels.

4
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.550
Then, early one morning, a
coach rolls across a bridge.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:18.200
From the coach, a poet writes: "Earth has
not anything to show more fair:" Wordsworth

6
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.990
is a poet of nature.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.020
So why would he call this city fair?

8
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.910
In this mission, you'll ride across
Westminster Bridge with William and Dorothy

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.640
Wordsworth, on 31 July 1802.

10
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:34.300
You'll hunt for what a nature
poet finds in this city view.

11
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.040
And you'll find the turn at line 9, where
the sonnet moves from what he sees to

12
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.670
what he feels.

13
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: explain why
Wordsworth calls London fair.
